      "message": "This seems a bit limiting.  Could we do the following instead?\n\n* When parsing config, if the user specifies a string, use regex, otherwise just store the value.\n* Here, check whether the expected value is a ZuulRegex instance, and if so, perform this string check and match; and if not, perform the old simple equality check.\n\nI think it would be useful to be able to match on boolean fields, etc. (I\u0027m imagining something like \"final: true\").",
